### O3 · /home/lingxufeng/bot/app/ui/main/dsh/connect.ts:81 · minor · CONFIRMED

- **summary**：stop() 无法阻止正在进行的连接完成并重新发布 socket。
- **触发条件**：start() 或定时重连已经进入 connectOnce()、尚在等待 token 交换或 socket.openPromise 时调用 stop()。connectOnce() 在 await 前后均不检查 stopped，随后仍安装 socket、增加 generation 并放行 readyWaiters。以延迟 fetch 重现：start() 后立即 stop()，再完成交换，最终 generation 为 1 且新 socket 未关闭。
- **失败表现**：停止操作完成后仍可能建立并保留活动连接、发布就绪结果；stop() 只关闭调用当时的 this.socket，无法清理之后才创建或完成握手的 socket。连接关闭与启动并发时失去停止保证。
- **verifier 证据**：File introduced by this diff: app/ui/main/dsh/connect.ts added in 22f806f (U-00) within b634e9d..aa9d934 — confirmed via git log on the path. Premise check: (1) connect.ts:77-89 connectOnce() contains no this.stopped check anywhere; its two await points are :78 (exchangeLaunchToken fetch) and :81 (socket.openPromise); after both it unconditionally runs :82-88 — closes old socket, installs this.socket = socket (:83), this.generation += 1 (:84), registers onDead (:85-87), resolves readyWaiters (:88). (2) stop() (connect.ts:118-122) only sets stopped, clears the reconnect timer, and closes this.socket as of call time — on a first/in-flight connect this.socket is undefined, so nothing gets closed. (3) The only stopped guard in the class is scheduleReconnect (connect.ts:92), which does not cover an in-flight connectOnce. (4) socket.ts:103-107 close() only affects the instance it is called on, so the later-installed socket is never closed. (5) No caller guarantee blocks the trigger: grep of app/ui shows no production caller of DshConnection.stop() at all — main/index.ts:97-98 starts the connection and :130-132 relies on app.quit() (process exit); the only callers are tests connect.test.ts:76 and :89, both after await conn.start() resolves, so no current in-repo path races. Experiment (mktemp /dev/shm sandbox, node --experimental-strip-types on a copy of the real connect.ts with only the './socket' import given a .ts extension and ws stubbed; real DshConnection logic byte-identical): start() → stop() while fetch pending → resolve fetch → resolve openPromise ⇒ output: 'stop() called; generation = 0', 'start resolved with generation = 1 (generation bumped after stop: true)', 'new socket closed by stop? false', 'ready() after stop returns live socket? true' — exactly the claimed failure (active socket survives stop, generation advances, ready result published; a later rpc() would proceed on a stopped connection). Verdict: race is real, unguarded, introduced by this change. Severity stays minor: currently unreachable from production flows (stop() has no production caller; app.quit() kills the process and the socket with it) and self-limiting — once the leaked socket dies, onDead → scheduleReconnect hits the stopped guard at connect.ts:92, so there is no reconnect loop, just one leaked live socket and one spurious generation bump.
- **finder**：sol:sweep

